## API Guide

This project was created **without a database**, so it uses an in-memory `MockRepository` (wired in `cmd/main.go`) to satisfy the service. Data is **not durable** — it resets every time the process restarts. Add a database with `gopamin new … -d <database>` for persistence.

The API is served under `http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users` (the port is `PORT` in `.env`, default `8080`).
{{if .Auth}}
### Authentication

Every `/users` route requires a JWT **bearer token** — without one you get `401`. Get a token from the demo login endpoint (credentials are `AUTH_USERNAME` / `AUTH_PASSWORD` in `.env`):

```text
curl --location --request POST 'http://localhost:8080/login' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
--data '{"username": "admin", "password": "change-me"}'
# -> {"token":"<JWT>"}
```

Add `--header 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'` to every request below.
{{end}}
### List Users (cursor-paginated)

```text
curl --location 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users?limit=20'{{if .Auth}} \
--header 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'{{end}}
```

The list is **cursor-paginated**: `?limit=N` bounds the page (default `20`, max `100`). When more rows remain, the response carries a `next_cursor` — pass it back as `?cursor=<next_cursor>` to fetch the next page (an opaque token; do not build it yourself).

### Add A New User

```text
curl --location 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json'{{if .Auth}} \
--header 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'{{end}} \
--data '{"name": "John Doe"}'
```

### Fetch An Existing User

```text
curl --location 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/<USER_ID>'{{if .Auth}} \
--header 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'{{end}}
```

### Update An Existing User

```text
curl --location --request PUT 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/<USER_ID>' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/json'{{if .Auth}} \
--header 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'{{end}} \
--data '{"name": "Jane Doe"}'
```

### Delete An Existing User

```text
curl --location --request DELETE 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/<USER_ID>'{{if .Auth}} \
--header 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'{{end}}
```
{{if .OpenAPI}}
### API Documentation (Swagger)

The app serves its own API docs — no external tooling needed:

- **Swagger UI** (interactive, "try it out"): `http://localhost:8080/swagger/`
- **Raw OpenAPI spec**: `http://localhost:8080/openapi.yaml`

The spec lives at `internal/adapters/api/openapi.yaml` — update it when you add or change a route.
{{end}}{{if .Broker}}
### Events

On a write (creating a user), the service publishes an event to **{{.Broker}}**, and a consumer loop runs alongside the HTTP server logging received messages. See the "Broker workflow" section of `AGENTS.md`.

**{{.Broker}} runs in a container**: start it with `make docker-up` before `make run`, or the app cannot reach the broker. `make docker-down` stops it (`make docker-down-rm-vol` also drops the volume).
{{end}}{{if .Observability}}
### Observability

`make docker-up` also starts an **OpenTelemetry Collector** (config: `configs/otel-collector.yaml`). The app exports traces and metrics to it over OTLP — see the `OTEL_*` keys in `.env`. With the collector running, requests appear as spans in its debug output.
{{end}}